<!--END ADD DESMOS INTERATIVE-->
<div class="os-raise-student-reflection">
  <para class="os-raise-student-reflection-title">Building Character: Growth Mindset</para>
  <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-gap-1">
    <figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/73874f1a255999b5120ed446429bafe1e18ea4c2"/></media></figure><div>
      <para class="os-raise-mb-0">Compared to a fixed mindset, a growth mindset encourages you to embrace challenges, sustain effort, and try new strategies. Of course, no one embodies only a growth or fixed mindset; we are all a mixture of the two, and we can learn to recognize what triggers a fixed versus growth mindset. The brain is like a muscle—something you can strengthen.</para>
      <para>Think about your current sense of having a growth mindset. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
      <list>
        <item>
          I truly believe that people can change.
        </item>
        <item>
          I can always change how intelligent I am.
        </item>
      </list>
      <para>Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
     </div>
  </div>
</div></section>
